Bilibili video summary for DeepSeek Harness

Original work by the dsh-zcode-plugins contributors, MIT licensed.

What this plugin talks to:

- Bilibili web APIs (`api.bilibili.com`): `x/web-interface/view` for metadata,
  `x/v2/subtitle/web/view` for the subtitle track list, `x/player/wbi/playurl`
  for the audio fallback, and `x/web-interface/view/conclusion/get` for the
  platform's own AI summary.
- Bilibili's official passport QR flow (`passport.bilibili.com`):
  `x/passport-login/web/qrcode/generate` issues the login code and
  `x/passport-login/web/qrcode/poll` reports scan progress and sets the session
  cookies. The plugin renders the login URL as a PNG locally; it never sends the
  code to a third-party image service.
- `aisubtitle.hdslb.com` for the subtitle JSON a track points at, after the
  `subtitle.bilibili.com` path is decoded and rewritten.

The credentials stay local: the cookie jar is written to
`$DSH_HOME/bilibili-cookies.json` (mode 0600) and is only ever sent to
`bilibili.com` hosts. `bilibili_login { action: "logout" }` deletes it.

Subtitle route notes: `x/v2/subtitle/web/view` answers in protobuf, and the
paths it returns must be XOR-decoded and re-hosted before they can be fetched.
The two key pairs used for that transform are transcribed from Bilibili's own
player bundle (`bfs/static/player/main/core.*.js`, the `F`/`U` helpers); the
plugin reimplements the same transform in `lib/subtitle-url.js` and pins it with
a unit test. The legacy `x/player/v2` subtitle field is deliberately not used:
under rate limiting it has been observed returning a truncated body belonging
to another video.

No-subtitle fallback: Bcut (必剪) is the default and needs no local model. If
Bcut rejects the audio, the plugin can reuse an already-installed
faster-whisper runtime (`$DSH_HOME/bilibili-asr/venv` and `models`) or install
one only after the user chooses persistent/temporary mode. No faster-whisper
package, virtualenv, or model is bundled. Temporary audio files are removed
after transcription.

Third-party code:

- `qrcode-generator` (MIT, Kazuhiko Arase) renders the sign-in QR modules.
- `faster-whisper` is installed into the fallback virtualenv at runtime; it is
  not bundled with this package.
- ffmpeg is used as an external binary for audio extraction; it is not bundled.
- Everything else is Node standard library plus the bundled Python script.

